---
import Section from "../../components/Section.astro";
import { mailto, site } from "../../data/site";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "13 October 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Xplit Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Xplit (Expense Splitter) by Visify Apps."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/xplit"
>
  <Section narrow>
    <p class="label">Legal · Xplit</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">
      Updated {lastUpdated} · Package <code>com.visify.xplit</code>
    </p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>Xplit</strong> (Expense
        Splitter), published by {site.shortName}, handles information. Xplit is
        designed to be <strong>local-first</strong>: day-to-day expense data
        stays on your device unless you choose optional cloud backup.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information we process</h2>
      <h3>1.1 On your device (local)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Group names, member names, expenses, settlements, budgets, and related
          notes you enter
        </li>
        <li>App preferences (for example theme and widget settings)</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This data is stored in a local database on your phone. {site.shortName}
        cannot read it unless you use optional cloud backup.
      </p>

      <h3>1.2 Optional account &amp; cloud backup</h3>
      <p>If you sign in for cloud backup, we process:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Email address and authentication credentials (via Firebase
          Authentication)
        </li>
        <li>
          A backup snapshot of your local groups/expenses (stored in Cloud
          Firestore under your user id)
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>Backup is optional. You can use Xplit without an account.</p>

      <h3>1.3 Advertising (Android)</h3>
      <p>
        The App shows ads through <strong>Google AdMob</strong>. Google and its
        partners may collect device and advertising identifiers, IP address,
        approximate location derived from IP, interaction data, and diagnostic
        information to serve and measure ads, including personalized ads where
        allowed. You may see options related to ad personalization based on your
        region and device settings.
      </p>
      <p>
        See Google’s
        <a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">Privacy Policy</a
        >
        and
        <a
          href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          target="_blank">AdMob &amp; privacy</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h3>1.4 Diagnostics</h3>
      <p>
        Standard platform services (for example Google Play services / Firebase)
        may collect crash or technical diagnostics as configured by those SDKs.
        We do not sell your personal information.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To provide core expense-splitting features on your device</li>
        <li>To provide optional backup/restore if you sign in</li>
        <li>To show ads and keep the App free</li>
        <li>To improve reliability and security</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Sharing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Firebase</strong> — optional auth and backup</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google AdMob / advertising partners</strong> — ads and
          measurement
        </li>
        <li>We do not sell personal data to data brokers</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Retention</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Local data remains until you delete it in the App or uninstall the App
        </li>
        <li>
          Cloud backup remains until you delete the backup/account or request
          deletion
        </li>
        <li>Ad-related data is retained per Google’s policies</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the App without signing in</li>
        <li>Delete groups or reset/delete data in the App</li>
        <li>
          Delete your account / backup from the backup settings (where
          available)
        </li>
        <li>
          Adjust device ad / privacy settings, or use the in-app rewarded option
          to pause ads temporarily when offered
        </li>
        <li>
          Email us to request help with account or backup deletion:
          <a href={mailto("Xplit privacy / deletion")}>{site.email}</a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. Children</h2>
      <p>
        Xplit is not directed at children under 13 (or the minimum age required
        in your country). We do not knowingly collect personal information from
        children.
      </p>

      <h2>7. International processing</h2>
      <p>
        If you use Firebase or AdMob, data may be processed on servers outside
        your country, including by Google, subject to their safeguards and
        applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. The “Updated” date at the top will change when
        we do. Continued use of the App after an update means you accept the
        revised policy.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {site.shortName}<br />
        Email: <a href={mailto("Xplit privacy")}>{site.email}</a><br />
        App: Xplit — Expense Splitter (<code>com.visify.xplit</code>)
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/privacy">← Company privacy</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .meta {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
  }
</style>
